    "url": "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/wargamingen/jobs/8066793",
    "desc": "Job Overview\n\nWargaming Belgrade is looking for a creative 2D Artist who thrives on variety, enjoys early-stage visual development, and sees constraints as an opportunity for innovation.\nIn this role, creativity is your strongest asset. You will explore visual directions, develop concepts, and shape the mood and atmosphere of in-game events and marketing initiatives from the earliest stages.\nOur 2D Art team is responsible for the visual identity of the World of Warships franchise, creating everything from marketing key art and in-game store graphics to client-facing content, backgrounds, animatics, and skins.\nWhile our visual style is grounded in realistic naval art, built on photobash and 3D foundations, we're looking for someone who can bring fresh ideas and a strong artistic vision. You will take creative ownership of complex tasks, develop visual solutions from scratch, collaborate closely with Art Directors, and help shape the creative direction of our projects.\n\nReports to\n\n2D Team Lead\n\nWhat will you do?\n\n•\nIllustrations: create high-quality promotional illustrations, produce polished art for in-game shops and publishing, including loading screens, banners, previews, event backgrounds, and special offer images\n\n•\nVisual Development: early sketches for events and marketing campaigns. Some skins concepts (in case of ships it’s a mix of hard surf and environment concept art)\n\n•\nWorkflow Execution: utilize photobash, matte painting, and 3D renders (Blender) to build detailed, realistic scenes with ships, environments, and props. Most often, 3D models will be provided by the 3D team\n\n•\nCreative Ownership: take full ownership of your work from the sketch phase to final polish, with minimal guidance and strong attention to detail\n\n•\nIn-House Collaboration: prepare sketches and concept drafts to pass to teammates for further refinement. Work closely with the Art Director, publishing teams, and other departments to propose visual solutions and ensure alignment\n\n•\nProblem Solving: identify design challenges quickly and propose creative, practical solutions during art reviews and collaborative meetings\n\nWhat are we looking for?\n\n•\n3+ years of experience working as a Concept Artist, 2D Artist, or Illustrator in the GameDev industry\n\n•\nExpert-level skills in Adobe Photoshop\n\n•\nHands-on experience with 3D software (ideally Blender) to block out scenes, set lighting, and render bases for overpaint\n\n•\nExcellent understanding of composition, lighting, color theory, perspective, and design principles, with the ability to clearly convey form and atmosphere\n\n•\nExperienced with matte painting and photobash techniques\n\n•\nUpper-Intermediate (B2) or higher English knowledge\n\nWhat additional skills will help you stand out?\n\n•\nStronger 3D skills: modeling, texturing, or sculpting (e.g., ZBrush, 3D-Coat).\n\n•\nExperience giving precise, structured, and constructive art feedback to in-house team members\n\n•\nAbility to adapt to different art styles when needed (realistic, semi-realistic, stylized)\n\n•\nExceptional sketching skills for storyboards and quick proof-of-concept designs\n\n•\nAAA experience is a strong plus\n\nWhat would we like to see in your portfolio?\n\n•\nA portfolio showcasing realistic or semi-realistic concept design, environments, and cinematic key art\n\nWork mode\n\n•\nDuring the probation period: onsite\n\n•\nAfter the probation period: onsite or hybrid (3 days per week in Belgrade office)\n\n•\nThis role is eligible for relocation & immigration support\n\nBenefits\n\nBenefits and perks are tailored to the local market and culture. Our benefits in Belgrade include:\n\n•\nAdditional vacation days based on years of service at Wargaming: up to 5 days on top of the statutory minimum\n\n•\nAdditional paid time off (5 Personal Days, Birthday Leave, Marriage Leave, Compassionate Leave)\n\n•\nSick Leave Compensation, Maternity Leave Benefits\n\n•\nPremium Private Health Insurance\n\n•\nCareer development and education opportunities within the company\n\n•\nEnglish clubs and platform for learning languages\n\n•\nMental well-being program (iFeel)\n\n•\nCommuting allowance\n\n•\nCompany events\n\n•\nFitPass membership\n\n•\nDiscounts for employees\n\n•\nPersonal Gaming Account\n\n•\nCoffee, fruits, and snacks in the office\n\n•\nOn-site canteen with subsidized prices for food and drinks\n\n•\nSeniority Awards\n\n•\nReferral program - you can recommend the best talents to the Company and receive a reward\n\nPlease submit your CV in English to ensure smooth processing and review.\nAbout Wargaming\n\nWargaming is an award-winning online game developer and publisher headquartered in Nicosia, Cyprus. Operating since 1998, Wargaming has become one of the leaders in the gaming industry with 15 offices worldwide, including studios in Chicago, Prague, Shanghai, Tokyo, and Vilnius. Our diverse and multicultural team works together to deliver a top-class experience to millions of players who enjoy Wargaming's titles across all major gaming platforms. Our flagship products include free-to-play hits World of Tanks, World of Warships and World of Tanks Blitz.\n\nPlease see Wargaming Candidate Privacy Policy for details on how Wargaming uses your personal data.",
