    "url": "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/wargamingen/jobs/8078945",
    "desc": "Job Overview\n\nWe are looking for a Middle Frontend Developer to join the Global Content team and work on interactive web projects and portal game mechanics for World of Warships.\n\nYou will be involved in developing and supporting the multilingual and multi-regional World of Warships portal: event pages, web adventures, interactive mechanics, mini-games, visual-heavy interfaces, and portal modules that support in-game events and the overall ecosystem of the project.\n\nThis is a hybrid role at the intersection of interactive frontend development, CMS-driven solutions, and production web development. A large part of the current production codebase is built with vanilla JavaScript, so a strong understanding of native frontend development and browser APIs is important for this role. At the same time, you will participate in expanding Vue 3 usage as a foundation for new solutions and the potential migration of existing projects.\n\nWe are looking for a developer who enjoys building non-standard interactive web mechanics, working with animations and complex frontend behavior, while maintaining stability, performance, and production quality.\n\nWhat will you do?\n\n•\nDevelop and maintain event pages, web adventures, game web mechanics, mini-games, widgets, and portal/web modules\n\n•\nDevelop frontend solutions using Vue 3, TypeScript, and related tooling\n\n•\nWork with production code written in vanilla JavaScript\n\n•\nWork with REST APIs, JSON configurations, and data-driven interfaces\n\n•\nImplement complex animations and interactive behavior\n\n•\nWork with visual-heavy and interactive web interfaces\n\n•\nPrepare and maintain frontend bundles for CMS integration\n\n•\nOptimize performance of animation-heavy and mobile-heavy pages: asset loading, rendering, lazy loading, browser behavior, and frontend performance\n\n•\nEnsure proper functionality across different devices, browsers, regional versions, and language configurations\n\n•\nCollaborate with designers using Figma, verify implementations, and prepare/export assets when needed\n\n•\nSupport and improve reusable components, UI patterns, and shared frontend approaches\n\n•\nWrite technical documentation and implementation guidelines\n\nWhat are we looking for?\n\n•\n3+ years of commercial frontend development experience with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n\n•\nStrong knowledge of JavaScript (ES6+) and browser APIs\n\n•\nStrong HTML5, CSS3, and SCSS skills\n\n•\n2+ years of practical experience with Vue 3\n\n•\nExperience with TypeScript and Composition API\n\n•\nExperience with mobile web development\n\n•\nStrong practical understanding of cross-browser compatibility and platform/browser quirks\n\n•\nExperience working with REST APIs, JSON, and asynchronous client-server interactions\n\n•\nExperience implementing complex animations and interactive interfaces\n\n•\nExperience working with CMS or content-driven web projects\n\n•\nIndependence in solving technical tasks and finding solutions\n\n•\nAttention to implementation quality, interface details, and user experience\n\n•\nAbility to work across different types of tasks and contexts\n\n•\nAbility to work with existing codebases, refactor code, and maintain production quality\n\n•\nConfident use of Figma\n\n•\nEnglish sufficient for technical communication and documentation\n\nWhat additional skills will help you stand out?\n\n•\nGood sense of visual design, composition, and understanding of UI/UX principles for interactive web interfaces (previous design experience would be a plus)\n\n•\nExperience with Three.js, WebGL, or other 3D/web graphics solutions\n\n•\nExperience with GSAP, ScrollTrigger, and similar solutions\n\n•\nExperience with Pinia and Vite\n\n•\nExperience working with web analytics or tracking systems\n\n•\nExperience with Node.js in the context of frontend tooling, scripts, and build systems\n\n•\nExperience working with design systems or custom UI kits\n\n•\nUnderstanding of frontend performance optimization and browser rendering\n\n•\nUnderstanding of frontend bundles and build/deploy flows for CMS integration\n\n•\nBasic understanding of frontend delivery pipelines: Nginx, CDN, Object Storage, GitLab CI/CD\n\n•\nBasic Photoshop skills\n\n•\nExperience working on multilingual and multi-regional projects\n\n•\nRussian language skills\n\n•\nLinks to relevant projects: interactive pages, mini-games, animation-heavy, or 3D/web-heavy cases\n\nWork mode\n\n• Onsite during probation period and hybrid after probation period (3 days of work from the office and 2 days of work form home).\n\nBenefits\n\nBenefits and perks are tailored to the local market and culture. Our benefits in Belgrade include:\n\n• Additional vacation days based on years of service at Wargaming: up to 5 days on top of the statutory minimum\n\n• Additional paid time off (5 Personal Days, Birthday Leave, Marriage Leave, Compassionate Leave)\n\n• Sick Leave Compensation, Maternity Leave Benefits\n\n• Premium Private Health Insurance\n\n• Career development and education opportunities within the company\n\n• English clubs and platform for learning languages\n\n• Mental well-being program (iFeel)\n\n• Commuting allowance\n\n• Company events\n\n• FitPass membership\n\n• Discounts for employees\n\n• Personal Gaming Account\n\n• Coffee, fruits, and snacks in the office\n\n• On-site canteen with subsidized prices for food and drinks\n\n• Seniority Awards\n\n• Referral program - you can recommend the best talents to the Company and receive a reward\n\nPlease submit your CV in English to ensure smooth processing and review.\n\nAbout Wargaming…",
