    "url": "https://jobs.lever.co/amanotes/6d610a18-1bf2-4954-9785-15a727c4c27c",
    "desc": "\nABOUT THE ROLE\nObjective:\n\n•\nLead the product strategy and execution for Amanotes’ Music Apps portfolio, co-owning the product vision, roadmap, and business outcomes (growth, engagement, monetization) end-to-end.\n\n•\nPartner with the Head of Music App and cross-functional leaders to define the multi-year direction for Music Apps, then translate it into clear bets, roadmaps, and experiments that deliver measurable results at scale.\n\nOutcomes:\n\n• Co-own the Music Apps product vision and 1–3 year roadmap with the Head of Music App, making clear strategic choices on which user problems, markets, and business opportunities to prioritize.\n\n• Own the business performance of Music Apps (revenue, ARPDAU, subscriptions, LTV/CAC, profitability).\n\n• Build, lead, and coach a high-performing product team (PMs, cross-functional squads) with clear goals, ownership, and growth paths.\n\n• Shape and continuously improve the operating model for Music Apps (cadence, decision-making, experimentation, quality bar)\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n• Define and drive the product strategy for Music Apps, from market and user insights to clear product bets, success metrics, and portfolio priorities.\n\n• Co-lead the Music Apps roadmap with the Head of Music Apps, balancing short-term wins and long-term strategic investments.\n\n• Own prioritization across squads and initiatives, making explicit trade-offs on scope, quality, and speed to maximize business impact.\n\n• Lead and mentor POs in the Music Apps domain, ensuring strong product thinking, execution, and growth.\n\n• Represent Music Apps in key company forums (planning, reviews, investment discussions), aligning stakeholders and securing resources.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\nMust Have:\n\n• 3-5+ years of experience as a Product Manager (or similar role) for consumer mobile apps (B2C), ideally in entertainment, lifestyle, productivity, or content-based apps.\n\n• Strong experience building and scaling mobile apps for global markets (multiple countries/regions, app stores, and user segments).\n\n• Proven track record of shipping features or products end-to-end – from discovery and specification to launch and iteration – with measurable business impact.\n\n• Strong skills in problem framing, product discovery, and translating ideas into clear product requirements and roadmaps.\n\n• Solid understanding of mobile app metrics and growth (activation, funnels, retention, cohorts, engagement, monetization, LTV/CAC).\n\n• Experience working with cross-functional teams (Engineering, Design, Data, Marketing) in an agile or iterative development environment.\n\n• Ability to work both strategically and hands-on: from understanding high-level vision to reviewing detailed flows, copy, and builds.\n\n• Strong analytical skills: comfortable working with data, setting up basic analyses, and using insights to drive decisions.\n\n• Excellent communication and stakeholder management, able to create alignment and clarity across teams.\n\n• Professional working proficiency in English (both written and spoken).\n\nNice to Have:\n\n• Experience with music-tech, or gaming apps, or other live-service products.\n\n• Familiarity with in-app purchases and/or subscription models on iOS and Android.\n\n• Experience running A/B tests and growth experiments in consumer apps.\n\n• Background or strong interest in music (e.g., playing an instrument, DJing, producing, or deep passion for music and music apps).\n\n• Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth tech or mobile company.\n\nBENEFITS\nAt Amanotes, you will be enjoying the dynamic working environment with unique music culture many benefits as below:\n\n• Competitive salary upon experience\n\n• 13th month salary\n\n• Year-end Bonus\n\n• Flexible working time\n\n• Personal learning and well-being budget\n\n• Team-building budget\n\n• Lunch and parking allowance\n\n• Various learning activities, including internal training & sharing, international conferences, and e-learning (Udemy, LinkedIn Learning...).\n\n• Engaging music events: Music Night, Amasing Night, Music schools…\n\n• Employee Assistance Program to support mental health & well-being.\n\n• 12 days of paid annual leave, plus 10 days of paid sick leave.\n\n• 12 days working from home per year.\nConsent Notice for Personal Data Processing\n- By applying to any position at Amanotes, you acknowledge and agree that your personal data will be collected and processed for recruitment-related purposes. Please read the “Consent Notice for Personal Data Processing” carefully before submitting your application.\n- Thank you for your interest in joining Amanotes.\n\nAbout Amanotes\n\nWe are Amanotes – a dynamic music game company that’s using cutting-edge technology to transform how people experience music.\n\nSince 2014, we’ve led the global simple music game market with over 3.5 billion downloads across 190+ countries, including chart-topping titles like Magic Tiles 3, Tiles Hop, Dancing Road, and Duet Cats.\n\nAs the #1 Music Game Publisher worldwide and the #1 App Publisher from Southeast Asia by downloads, our ambition is clear: to create iconic, hybrid-casual music games that people love and play for years.\n\nWhat truly sets Amanotes apart is not just what we build — it’s how we grow and who we grow with:\n\n🎓 We invest in your growth through learning budgets, coaching, and stretch opportunities.\n\n🎶 We embrace a creative and dynamic culture, where everyone can play, share, and thrive.\n\n🧘 We believe in work-life harmony — your rhythm matters here.\n\n🏆 We recognize and reward impact, with competitive benefits and clear development paths.\n\nCome join our music-filled workplace, where innovation meets rhythm — and let’s create a magical music experience together.\n\nAmanotes – Where Everyone Can Music.\n\nHow To Apply?\n\nClick the button or contact us at talents@amanotes.com.",
